		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4589&amp;p=34131#p34131"><![CDATA[
@Colin.<br><br>Thank you very much for your help in clarifying the way to create a fresh codeplug.  <br><br>Having defined my contacts, I prepared several TG lists using one for each teams A, B &amp; &amp; C, etc. and then set about defining several channels for each repeatereach calling up one TG list.  This linked Repeater 1 to TG Lists A, B &amp; C (3 channels) and Repeater 2 to TG Lists A, B &amp; C.and so forth.<br><br>I then created Zones for each team, so that I could work the team I wanted and could switch between repeaters easily.  Zone A contains all Team A channels, Zone B, all B channels and so on.<br><br>Sorry if that looks a bit complex, but I envision it as a form of matrix with zones horizontally and teams vertically with the channels in the middle with a third dimension of contacts.  I really must get a life!<br><br>Colin, you have been great. Many thanks again.<br>73 Keith<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7005">G4WQB</a> — Mon Nov 18, 2024 4:20 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
