		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4589&amp;p=34106#p34106"><![CDATA[
You can only have one TG List allocated to a channel. So in your case you could have three channels, one for Aylesbury, one for Tring, and one for West London. All three channels could be linked to the same TG List containing all of the DMR+ (Phoenix) talkgroups.  <br><br>If you need to use a different TG list you would need to define a new channel that is linked to that list. So you may need Aylesbury A , Aylesbury B, and Aylesbury C. <br><br>Colin G4EML<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Sat Nov 16, 2024 12:22 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
